{"title":"Median (statistics)","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>median</b> is a measure of central tendency used frequently in statistics.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Median_of_a_data_set\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Median of a data set</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Median_of_a_distribution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Median of a distribution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Discrete_distributions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Discrete distributions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Continuous_distributions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Continuous distributions</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Introductory\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introductory</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Intermediate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Olympiad\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Olympiad</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Median_of_a_data_set\">Median of a data set</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Median_(statistics)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Median of a data set\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The median of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Finite\" title=\"Finite\">finite</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Set\" title=\"Set\">set</a> of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real numbers</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/613ff6609f8a69908e31023a62deb8808d417794.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{X_1, ..., X_k\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" /> is defined to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4be9a811cd45d42e1df9bfeab8268a4aa00c19f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^k |X_i - x| = \\min_y \\sum_{i=1}^k |X_i - y|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"238\" height=\"51\" />. This turns out to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/b/5eb183fdf3aab50f340d2136b587b4ee2923c760.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_{(\\frac{k+1}2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"49\" height=\"21\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is odd. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is even, all points between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/b/e1b3642a33a6c3d89d55b2c591e3ad7debf046a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_{(\\frac{k}2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"34\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7cb2cc9983ab28dad120cd5c688a581b9c8393.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_{(\\frac{k}2 + 1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> are medians. If we have to specify one median we conventionally take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/e/15e5a65afcdde2f91f2291caee53c9047c80a9e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{X_{(\\frac{k}2)} + X_{(\\frac{k}2 + 1)}}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"114\" height=\"40\" />. (Here <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/c/25c1ad06357dd6990f10605591b624655e7516ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_{(i)}, i \\in \\{1,...,k\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"19\" /> denotes the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f95e9fc37dc276d9cfc43aba335cde356371cac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^{th}$\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Order_statistic&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Order statistic (page does not exist)\">order statistic</a>.) For example, the median of the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/5/615e2d6960662169ca6d7f8c2a70d56634b73ba8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" /> is 7.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Median_of_a_distribution\">Median of a distribution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Median_(statistics)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Median of a distribution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Discrete_distributions\">Discrete distributions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Median_(statistics)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Discrete distributions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discrete_distribution&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Discrete distribution (page does not exist)\">discrete distribution</a>, whose <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Support&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Support (page does not exist)\">support</a> is a subset of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Countable\" title=\"Countable\">countable</a> set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/6/a36c1ee0bcdad414dc8d3f129b1a0afcea556c4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${x_1, x_2, x_3, ...}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"13\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/2/342e2f11dc5506b79637a5e8a5bb90dbcdf68d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i &lt; x_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, the median of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is any point lying between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/c/b5c170dc53fce7452e6f7df461222672d913e34e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/4/454b8feffc06d1ded3513957fab950116c6fa5ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x_i)\\leq\\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"80\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d52be1a7b3120569c2d7d9b0f418cb4a03d0cd71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x_{i+1})\\geq\\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"97\" height=\"37\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/5/705bd97d08b4ba231a3b8e6754ea8068a82928ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x_i)=\\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"80\" height=\"37\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is defined to be the median of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Continuous_distributions\">Continuous distributions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Median_(statistics)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Continuous distributions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Continuous_distribution&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Continuous distribution (page does not exist)\">continuous distribution</a>, whose support is a subset of the real numbers, the median of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is defined to be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecd654230dbb22f569db9e9cb6f10c8f936f77e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x)=\\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"74\" height=\"37\" />. Clearly, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Density\" title=\"Density\">density</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />, this is equivalent to saying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f79f5d0a8d2aa6e5f931814da0256e95eed9866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int^x_{-\\infty}f = \\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"84\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Median_(statistics)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introductory\">Introductory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Median_(statistics)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Introductory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>Find the median of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/e/f7ef480d0b619226d81140611f34837d0ce19ccf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{3, 4, 5, 15, 9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" />.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 14\">2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 14</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate\">Intermediate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Median_(statistics)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Olympiad\">Olympiad</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Median_(statistics)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Olympiad\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><i>This problem has not been edited in. Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Median_(statistics)&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video\">Video</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Median_(statistics)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//youtu.be/TkZvMa30Juo\">Video</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Median_(statistics)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mean_of_a_set\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mean of a set\">Mean of a set</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mode_of_a_set\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mode of a set\">Mode of a set</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Median_(statistics)&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018095314\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.051 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 220/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 616/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5988/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.730      1 -total\n 55.84%    6.550      1 Template:Problem\n 42.85%    5.027      1 Template:Stub\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3475:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018095314 and revision id 243236. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}